## 11. PHASED IMPLEMENTATION PLAN

### Phase 1: Laptop Setup (Week 1-4) — $0 Cost

**Infrastructure:**
- Single laptop (16GB RAM, i5/i7)
- 5 Android phones for testing
- Local network (WiFi hotspot if needed)

**Deliverables by Week:**

| Week | Deliverables | Validation |
|------|--------------|------------|
| 1 | • Database schema setup (PostgreSQL + TimescaleDB)<br>• NATS + Centrifugo running<br>• Basic Go API skeleton<br>• Android app login screen | `curl http://localhost:8080/health` returns 200 |
| 2 | • GPS telemetry ingestion<br>• Real-time map display<br>• Vehicle CRUD APIs<br>• Driver app home screen | 5 phones sending GPS every 5s, visible on map |
| 3 | • Trip management<br>• Geofencing engine<br>• Alert rules engine<br>• Web dashboard basics | Create geofence, enter with phone, receive alert |
| 4 | • OBD integration (ELM327)<br>• Video upload (compressed)<br>• Offline sync working<br>• MDM lockdown tested | Full trip with OBD data + video, device locked |

**Exact Commands to Start:**

```bash
# Day 1: Environment Setup
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y git golang-1.21 postgresql-16 redis-server

# Install Go manually if needed
wget https://go.dev/dl/go1.21.0.linux-amd64.tar.gz
sudo rm -rf /usr/local/go && sudo tar -C /usr/local -xzf go1.21.0.linux-amd64.tar.gz
echo 'export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/go/bin' >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc

# Day 1: Project Structure
mkdir -p ~/fleet-platform/{api-gateway,vehicle-service,tracking-service,trip-service,driver-service,alert-service,video-service,admin-web,android-driver,android-manager,docs}
cd ~/fleet-platform

# Initialize Go modules
for svc in api-gateway vehicle-service tracking-service trip-service driver-service alert-service video-service; do
    cd $svc && go mod init fleet.io/$svc && cd ..
done

# Day 1: Database
sudo -u postgres psql -c "CREATE DATABASE fleetdb;"
sudo -u postgres psql -c "CREATE USER fleet WITH ENCRYPTED PASSWORD 'fleet123';"
sudo -u postgres psql -c "GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE fleetdb TO fleet;"
sudo -u postgres psql fleetdb -c "CREATE EXTENSION postgis; CREATE EXTENSION timescaledb;"

# Day 2: NATS + Centrifugo (from Section 8.2)
# ... setup commands ...

# Day 3: First Service (tracking-service)
cd tracking-service
cat > main.go << 'EOF'
package main

import (
    "github.com/gin-gonic/gin"
    "github.com/nats-io/nats.go"
)

func main() {
    r := gin.Default()
    
    // NATS connection
    nc, _ := nats.Connect(nats.DefaultURL)
    defer nc.Close()
    
    // Telemetry endpoint (from devices)
    r.POST("/telemetry/gps", func(c *gin.Context) {
        var payload map[string]interface{}
        if err := c.BindJSON(&payload); err != nil {
            c.JSON(400, gin.H{"error": err.Error()})
            return
        }
        
        // Publish to NATS for processing
        data, _ := json.Marshal(payload)
        nc.Publish("fleet.telemetry.gps", data)
        
        c.JSON(202, gin.H{"status": "accepted"})
    })
    
    r.Run(":8081")
}
EOF

go mod tidy
go run main.go

# Test with curl
curl -X POST http://localhost:8081/telemetry/gps \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"vehicle_id":"test-123","lat":19.0760,"lng":72.8777,"speed":45}'

# Continue building other services following this pattern...
```

### Phase 2: VPS Migration (Week 5-6) — $5-10/month

**Target:** Hetzner CX11 (1 vCPU, 2GB RAM, 20GB NVMe) = ₹400/month or Contabo VPS S = ₹350/month

**Migration Steps:**

```bash
# 1. On Laptop: Backup database
pg_dump -h localhost -U fleet fleetdb > fleetdb_backup.sql

# 2. Buy VPS, SSH in
ssh root@your-vps-ip

# 3. Setup (same as Phase 1 but optimized for production)
apt update && apt install -y docker.io docker-compose

# 4. Docker Compose for easy management
cat > docker-compose.yml << 'EOF'
version: '3.8'
services:
  postgres:
    image: timescale/timescaledb:latest-pg16
    volumes:
      - postgres_data:/var/lib/postgresql/data
      - ./init.sql:/docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/init.sql
    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: fleetdb
      POSTGRES_USER: fleet
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${DB_PASSWORD}
    ports:
      - "127.0.0.1:5432:5432"
  
  nats:
    image: nats:latest
    command: "-js -m 8222 --mqtt_port 1883"
    ports:
      - "4222:4222"
      - "1883:1883"
      - "8222:8222"
    volumes:
      - nats_data:/data/jetstream
  
  redis:
    image: redis:7-alpine
    volumes:
      - redis_data:/data
  
  api-gateway:
    build: ./api-gateway
    ports:
      - "80:8080"
      - "443:8443"
    environment:
      - DATABASE_URL=postgres://fleet:${DB_PASSWORD}@postgres:5432/fleetdb?sslmode=disable
      - NATS_URL=nats://nats:4222
      - REDIS_URL=redis:6379
    depends_on:
      - postgres
      - nats
      - redis
  
  # Add other services similarly, or use single binary for resource constraints
  all-services:
    build: ./  # Single combined binary for Phase 2
    environment:
      - MODE=production
      - DATABASE_URL=postgres://fleet:${DB_PASSWORD}@postgres:5432/fleetdb?sslmode=disable
    ports:
      - "8080:8080"

volumes:
  postgres_data:
  nats_data:
  redis_data:
EOF

# 5. Restore database
docker-compose up -d postgres
sleep 10
docker exec -i fleet-platform_postgres_1 psql -U fleet fleetdb < fleetdb_backup.sql

# 6. Start all services
docker-compose up -d

# 7. Update Android apps to point to new server
# Change base URL in build.gradle:
# buildConfigField "String", "BASE_URL", "\"https://your-vps-ip/api/v1/\""
```

### Phase 3: Scalable Architecture (Month 3+) — $50-200

**When to Upgrade:**
- >500 vehicles (Phase 2 limit: ~500 on 2GB RAM)
- >50 concurrent video streams
- Need 99.9% uptime (SLA requirements)

**Architecture:**

```
┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐
│   Cloudflare│────▶│  K8s Ingress│────▶│  Go Services    │
│   (Free CDN)│     │  (Caddy)      │     │  (Auto-scaled)  │
└─────────────┘     └─────────────┘     └────────┬────────┘
                                                │
                       ┌─────────────────────────┼──────────┐
                       ▼                         ▼          ▼
              ┌─────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐
              │  Managed DB     │     │  Managed NATS   │  │  S3/MinIO    │
              │  (DigitalOcean  │     │  (Synadia Cloud   │  │  (Wasabi/    │
              │   or Scaleway)  │     │   free tier)      │  │   self-host) │
              └─────────────────┘     └─────────────────┘  └──────────────┘
```

