# FLEET MANAGEMENT SYSTEM SPECIFICATION

## Executive Summary

This specification delivers a Samsara-like fleet platform designed for Indian operations, scaling from 10 to 100,000+ vehicles. The architecture prioritizes low-cost self-hosting, offline-first mobile operation, and zero cloud dependencies while maintaining enterprise-grade reliability.

---

## 1. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE

### 1.1 High-Level Architecture Diagram

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                              EDGE LAYER (Vehicles)                          │
│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────┐ │
│  │ Android     │  │ OBD-II      │  │ Dashcam     │  │ Temperature Sensor  │ │
│  │ Driver App  │  │ Adapter     │  │ (Future)    │  │ (Future)            │ │
│  │             │  │ (Bluetooth) │  │             │  │                     │ │
│  │ • GPS 5s    │  │ • RPM       │  │ • AI Events │  │ • Cold chain        │ │
│  │ • Offline   │  │ • Fuel      │  │ • Streaming │  │ • Alerts            │ │
│  │ • SOS       │  │ • DTCs      │  │             │  │                     │ │
│  └──────┬──────┘  └──────┬──────┘  └─────────────┘  └─────────────────────┘ │
│         │                │                                                   │
│         └────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
│                          │ MQTT 3.1.1 (TLS) / HTTP/2 Fallback
│                          ▼
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                           GATEWAY LAYER (Single Laptop/Server)              │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │                         Traefik (TLS Termination)                       │ │
│  │                    • Auto HTTPS (Let's Encrypt)                         │ │
│  │                    • Rate Limiting • Circuit Breaker                    │ │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
│                                    │                                        │
│  ┌─────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │   NATS Server   │  │  Go API Server  │  │   Centrifugo (WebSocket)    │ │
│  │                 │  │                 │  │                             │ │
│  │ • MQTT 1883     │  │ • REST API      │  │ • Real-time to web          │ │
│  │ • JetStream     │  │ • gRPC Internal │  │ • 10k+ connections          │ │
│  │ • Persistence   │  │ • JWT Auth      │  │ • Fallback SSE              │ │
│  │ • Leaf Nodes    │  │ • RBAC          │  │                             │ │
│  └────────┬────────┘  └────────┬────────┘  └─────────────────────────────┘ │
│           │                    │                                           │
│  ┌────────┴────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │                      Data Layer (PostgreSQL + Redis)                  │ │
│  │  ┌─────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────┐    │ │
│  │  │ PostgreSQL 16   │  │ TimescaleDB     │  │ Redis 7             │    │ │
│  │  │ • Users/Roles   │  │ • GPS hypertable│  │ • Sessions          │    │ │
│  │  │ • Vehicles      │  │ • 1s resolution │  │ • Rate limits       │    │ │
│  │  │ • Trips         │  │ • 90d retention │  │ • Real-time pub/sub │    │ │
│  │  │ • Billing       │  │ • Compression   │  │ • Geo-spatial       │    │ │
│  │  └─────────────────┘  └─────────────────┘  └─────────────────────┘    │ │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                    │
                                    ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                           CLIENT LAYER                                      │
│  ┌─────────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────┐ │
│  │ Web Admin (React)   │  │ Fleet Manager App   │  │ External APIs       │ │
│  │                     │  │ (Android)           │  │                     │ │
│  │ • Live Map          │  │ • Dashboard         │  │ • Fastag (Future)   │ │
│  │ • Vehicle Mgmt      │  │ • Alerts            │  │ • E-way Bill        │ │
│  │ • Reports           │  │ • Approvals         │  │ • Insurance         │ │
│  │ • Settings          │  │ • Quick Actions     │  │                     │ │
│  └─────────────────────┘  └─────────────────────┘  └─────────────────────┘ │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 1.2 Component Responsibilities

| Component | Technology | Responsibility | Resource Usage |
|-----------|-----------|----------------|---------------|
| **Traefik** | Go | Reverse proxy, TLS, rate limiting | 50MB RAM |
| **NATS** | Go | MQTT broker, message queue, JetStream | 100MB RAM |
| **API Server** | Go 1.21 | Business logic, REST API, auth | 100MB RAM |
| **Centrifugo** | Go | WebSocket server for real-time | 50MB RAM |
| **PostgreSQL** | C | Relational data, users, vehicles | 200MB RAM |
| **TimescaleDB** | C | Time-series GPS, OBD data | 300MB RAM |
| **Redis** | C | Cache, sessions, pub/sub | 50MB RAM |

**Total Base Memory: ~850MB** (fits on 2GB laptop with headroom)

---

## 2. DATABASE SCHEMA

### 2.1 Complete Schema with Retention

**File: `migrations/001_initial.up.sql`**

```sql
-- Enable extensions
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "uuid-ossp";
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "postgis";
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "timescaledb";

-- ============================================
-- CORE TABLES (Relational)
-- ============================================

CREATE TABLE organizations (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    name VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    slug VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    type VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'fleet_owner' 
        CHECK (type IN ('fleet_owner', 'reseller', 'partner', 'white_label')),
    settings JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{
        "timezone": "Asia/Kolkata",
        "currency": "INR",
        "distance_unit": "km",
        "fuel_unit": "liters",
        "map_provider": "osm"
    }',
    billing_email VARCHAR(255),
    address JSONB,
    gst_number VARCHAR(20),
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    deleted_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    
    CONSTRAINT valid_gst CHECK (gst_number ~ '^[0-9]{2}[A-Z]{5}[0-9]{4}[A-Z]{1}[1-9A-Z]{1}Z[0-9A-Z]{1}$')
);

CREATE INDEX idx_organizations_slug ON organizations(slug) WHERE deleted_at IS NULL;

CREATE TABLE users (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    org_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organizations(id),
    email VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    phone VARCHAR(20),
    password_hash VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    role VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'viewer'
        CHECK (role IN ('super_admin', 'admin', 'fleet_manager', 'driver', 'viewer', 'partner')),
    status VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active' 
        CHECK (status IN ('active', 'suspended', 'invited', 'inactive')),
    mfa_enabled BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
    mfa_secret VARCHAR(255),
    permissions JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',
    profile JSONB DEFAULT '{
        "name": null,
        "emergency_contact": null,
        "license_number": null,
        "license_expiry": null
    }',
    last_login_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    failed_login_attempts INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    locked_until TIMESTAMPTZ,
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    deleted_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    
    UNIQUE(org_id, email),
    UNIQUE(org_id, phone) WHERE phone IS NOT NULL
);

CREATE INDEX idx_users_org_role ON users(org_id, role) WHERE status = 'active' AND deleted_at IS NULL;
CREATE INDEX idx_users_phone ON users(phone) WHERE phone IS NOT NULL;

CREATE TABLE vehicles (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    org_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organizations(id),
    registration_number VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
    chassis_number VARCHAR(17),
    engine_number VARCHAR(20),
    type VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'truck'
        CHECK (type IN ('truck', 'bus', 'car', 'bike', 'tempo', 'tractor', 'school_bus', 'ambulance')),
    make VARCHAR(100),
    model VARCHAR(100),
    year INTEGER CHECK (year BETWEEN 1900 AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM NOW()) + 1),
    fuel_type VARCHAR(20) CHECK (fuel_type IN ('diesel', 'petrol', 'cng', 'electric', 'hybrid', 'lpg')),
    status VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active' 
        CHECK (status IN ('active', 'inactive', 'maintenance', 'retired', 'sold')),
    current_driver_id UUID REFERENCES users(id),
    current_location GEOGRAPHY(POINT, 4326),
    last_location_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    last_speed DECIMAL(5,2),
    last_ignition BOOLEAN,
    odometer_km DECIMAL(10,2),
    fuel_capacity_liters DECIMAL(6,2),
    documents JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',
    metadata JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    deleted_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    
    UNIQUE(org_id, registration_number),
    CONSTRAINT valid_reg_number CHECK (
        registration_number ~ '^[A-Z]{2}[0-9]{2}[A-Z]{1,2}[0-9]{4}$' OR
        registration_number ~ '^[A-Z]{2}[0-9]{2}[A-Z]{3}[0-9]{4}$'
    )
);

CREATE INDEX idx_vehicles_org ON vehicles(org_id) WHERE deleted_at IS NULL;
CREATE INDEX idx_vehicles_location ON vehicles USING GIST(current_location) WHERE current_location IS NOT NULL;
CREATE INDEX idx_vehicles_driver ON vehicles(current_driver_id) WHERE current_driver_id IS NOT NULL;

-- Device registry for hardware management
CREATE TABLE devices (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    org_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organizations(id),
    vehicle_id UUID REFERENCES vehicles(id),
    device_type VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL 
        CHECK (device_type IN ('android_phone', 'obd_adapter', 'gps_tracker', 'dashcam', 'iot_sensor')),
    imei VARCHAR(20) UNIQUE,
    serial_number VARCHAR(100),
    model VARCHAR(100),
    firmware_version VARCHAR(50),
    api_key_hash VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    status VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active' 
        CHECK (status IN ('active', 'inactive', 'suspended', 'lost')),
    last_seen_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    ip_address INET,
    metadata JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',
    enrolled_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_devices_vehicle ON devices(vehicle_id) WHERE status = 'active';
CREATE INDEX idx_devices_imei ON devices(imei) WHERE imei IS NOT NULL;

-- ============================================
-- TIME-SERIES TABLES (TimescaleDB Hypertables)
-- ============================================

-- GPS readings: 1 point per 5 seconds per vehicle
-- 100 vehicles × 12 points/min × 60 min × 24h = 1.7M rows/day
CREATE TABLE gps_readings (
    time TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    vehicle_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES vehicles(id),
    device_id UUID REFERENCES devices(id),
    latitude DECIMAL(10, 8) NOT NULL CHECK (latitude BETWEEN -90 AND 90),
    longitude DECIMAL(11, 8) NOT NULL CHECK (longitude BETWEEN -180 AND 180),
    altitude DECIMAL(8, 2),
    speed DECIMAL(5, 2) CHECK (speed >= 0),
    heading DECIMAL(5, 2) CHECK (heading BETWEEN 0 AND 360),
    accuracy DECIMAL(5, 2),
    ignition BOOLEAN,
    odometer_km DECIMAL(10, 2),
    satellites INTEGER CHECK (satellites BETWEEN 0 AND 32),
    battery_level INTEGER CHECK (battery_level BETWEEN 0 AND 100),
    metadata JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'
);

SELECT create_hypertable('gps_readings', 'time', 
    chunk_time_interval => INTERVAL '1 day',
    if_not_exists => TRUE
);

CREATE INDEX idx_gps_vehicle_time ON gps_readings (vehicle_id, time DESC);
CREATE INDEX idx_gps_location ON gps_readings USING BRIN (time, vehicle_id);

-- Compression: 90% space savings after 7 days
ALTER TABLE gps_readings SET (
    timescaledb.compress,
    timescaledb.compress_segmentby = 'vehicle_id',
    timescaledb.compress_orderby = 'time DESC'
);

SELECT add_compression_policy('gps_readings', INTERVAL '7 days');
SELECT add_retention_policy('gps_readings', INTERVAL '1 year');

-- OBD readings: 1 point per 30 seconds
CREATE TABLE obd_readings (
    time TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    vehicle_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES vehicles(id),
    device_id UUID REFERENCES devices(id),
    rpm INTEGER CHECK (rpm >= 0),
    speed_kmh INTEGER CHECK (speed_kmh >= 0),
    coolant_temp_celsius DECIMAL(5, 2),
    engine_load_percent DECIMAL(5, 2) CHECK (engine_load_percent BETWEEN 0 AND 100),
    fuel_level_percent DECIMAL(5, 2) CHECK (fuel_level_percent BETWEEN 0 AND 100),
    throttle_position DECIMAL(5, 2) CHECK (throttle_position BETWEEN 0 AND 100),
    intake_air_temp DECIMAL(5, 2),
    mass_airflow DECIMAL(8, 2),
    dtcs TEXT[], -- Diagnostic Trouble Codes
    vin VARCHAR(17),
    metadata JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'
);

SELECT create_hypertable('obd_readings', 'time', chunk_time_interval => INTERVAL '1 day');
CREATE INDEX idx_obd_vehicle_time ON obd_readings (vehicle_id, time DESC);
SELECT add_compression_policy('obd_readings', INTERVAL '7 days');
SELECT add_retention_policy('obd_readings', INTERVAL '1 year');

-- Events: Alerts, geofence triggers, driver behavior
CREATE TABLE events (
    time TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    vehicle_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES vehicles(id),
    driver_id UUID REFERENCES users(id),
    event_type VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
    severity VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'info' 
        CHECK (severity IN ('info', 'warning', 'critical', 'emergency')),
    latitude DECIMAL(10, 8),
    longitude DECIMAL(11, 8),
    metadata JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',
    acknowledged_by UUID REFERENCES users(id),
    acknowledged_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    resolved_at TIMESTAMPTZ
);

SELECT create_hypertable('events', 'time', chunk_time_interval => INTERVAL '7 days');
CREATE INDEX idx_events_vehicle ON events (vehicle_id, time DESC);
CREATE INDEX idx_events_type ON events (event_type, time DESC) WHERE severity IN ('critical', 'emergency');
SELECT add_retention_policy('events', INTERVAL '2 years');

-- Trips: Aggregated journey data
CREATE TABLE trips (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    org_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organizations(id),
    vehicle_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES vehicles(id),
    driver_id UUID REFERENCES users(id),
    status VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'planned' 
        CHECK (status IN ('planned', 'in_progress', 'paused', 'completed', 'cancelled')),
    started_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    ended_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    start_location GEOGRAPHY(POINT, 4326),
    end_location GEOGRAPHY(POINT, 4326),
    route GEOGRAPHY(LINESTRING, 4326),
    distance_km DECIMAL(10, 2),
    duration_minutes INTEGER,
    max_speed DECIMAL(5, 2),
    avg_speed DECIMAL(5, 2),
    fuel_consumed_liters DECIMAL(8, 2),
    fuel_cost_inr DECIMAL(10, 2),
    idle_time_minutes INTEGER,
    alerts_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    events JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',
    waypoints JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',
    metadata JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_trips_vehicle ON trips(vehicle_id, started_at DESC);
CREATE INDEX idx_trips_org ON trips(org_id, status) WHERE status = 'in_progress';

-- Geofences
CREATE TABLE geofences (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    org_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organizations(id),
    name VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    type VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'circle' 
        CHECK (type IN ('circle', 'polygon', 'corridor')),
    geometry GEOGRAPHY NOT NULL,
    radius_meters INTEGER, -- For circle
    buffer_meters INTEGER, -- For corridor
    entry_alert BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,
    exit_alert BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,
    speed_limit INTEGER,
    active_hours JSONB, -- {"start": "09:00", "end": "18:00", "days": [1,2,3,4,5]}
    vehicles UUID[], -- Empty = all vehicles
    metadata JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',
    created_by UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    deleted_at TIMESTAMPTZ
);

CREATE INDEX idx_geofences_org ON geofences(org_id) WHERE deleted_at IS NULL;
CREATE INDEX idx_geofences_geom ON geofences USING GIST(geometry);

-- Geofence events
CREATE TABLE geofence_events (
    time TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    geofence_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES geofences(id),
    vehicle_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES vehicles(id),
    event_type VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL CHECK (event_type IN ('entry', 'exit')),
    location GEOGRAPHY(POINT, 4326),
    metadata JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'
);

SELECT create_hypertable('geofence_events', 'time', chunk_time_interval => INTERVAL '1 day');
SELECT add_retention_policy('geofence_events', INTERVAL '6 months');

-- ============================================
-- AUDIT & SYSTEM TABLES
-- ============================================

CREATE TABLE audit_logs (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    table_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    record_id UUID NOT NULL,
    action VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL CHECK (action IN ('INSERT', 'UPDATE', 'DELETE')),
    old_data JSONB,
    new_data JSONB,
    changed_by UUID REFERENCES users(id),
    changed_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    ip_address INET,
    user_agent TEXT
);

CREATE INDEX idx_audit_table_record ON audit_logs(table_name, record_id, changed_at DESC);

-- API rate limiting tracking
CREATE TABLE rate_limit_buckets (
    key VARCHAR(255) PRIMARY KEY,
    tokens INTEGER NOT NULL,
    last_update TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);

-- ============================================
-- INDIA-SPECIFIC TABLES
-- ============================================

CREATE TABLE fastag_transactions (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    vehicle_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES vehicles(id),
    transaction_id VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    toll_plaza_id VARCHAR(50),
    toll_plaza_name VARCHAR(255),
    toll_plaza_location GEOGRAPHY(POINT, 4326),
    highway_name VARCHAR(255),
    amount_inr DECIMAL(8, 2) NOT NULL,
    transaction_time TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    tag_id VARCHAR(50),
    meta JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_fastag_vehicle ON fastag_transactions(vehicle_id, transaction_time DESC);

-- ============================================
-- FUNCTIONS & TRIGGERS
-- ============================================

CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION update_updated_at_column()
RETURNS TRIGGER AS $$
BEGIN
    NEW.updated_at = NOW();
    RETURN NEW;
END;
$$ language 'plpgsql';

-- Apply to all tables with updated_at
CREATE TRIGGER update_organizations_updated_at BEFORE UPDATE ON organizations 
    FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION update_updated_at_column();
CREATE TRIGGER update_users_updated_at BEFORE UPDATE ON users 
    FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION update_updated_at_column();
CREATE TRIGGER update_vehicles_updated_at BEFORE UPDATE ON vehicles 
    FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION update_updated_at_column();

-- Soft delete helper
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION soft_delete(table_name text, record_id uuid)
RETURNS void AS $$
BEGIN
    EXECUTE format('UPDATE %I SET deleted_at = NOW() WHERE id = $1', table_name)
    USING record_id;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;

-- Vehicle location update trigger (updates vehicles table from gps_readings)
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION update_vehicle_location()
RETURNS TRIGGER AS $$
BEGIN
    UPDATE vehicles 
    SET current_location = ST_SetSRID(ST_MakePoint(NEW.longitude, NEW.latitude), 4326)::geography,
        last_location_at = NEW.time,
        last_speed = NEW.speed,
        last_ignition = NEW.ignition,
        updated_at = NOW()
    WHERE id = NEW.vehicle_id;
    RETURN NEW;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;

CREATE TRIGGER trigger_update_vehicle_location
    AFTER INSERT ON gps_readings
    FOR EACH ROW
    EXECUTE FUNCTION update_vehicle_location();

-- Geofence check trigger
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION check_geofence_violation()
RETURNS TRIGGER AS $$
DECLARE
    gf RECORD;
    is_inside BOOLEAN;
    was_inside BOOLEAN;
BEGIN
    -- Check all active geofences for this vehicle
    FOR gf IN 
        SELECT * FROM geofences 
        WHERE deleted_at IS NULL 
        AND (vehicles = '{}' OR NEW.vehicle_id = ANY(vehicles))
    LOOP
        -- Current state
        is_inside := ST_Covers(gf.geometry, ST_SetSRID(ST_MakePoint(NEW.longitude, NEW.latitude), 4326)::geography);
        
        -- Previous state (check last event)
        SELECT (event_type = 'entry') INTO was_inside
        FROM geofence_events
        WHERE geofence_id = gf.id AND vehicle_id = NEW.vehicle_id
        ORDER BY time DESC
        LIMIT 1;
        
        was_inside := COALESCE(was_inside, FALSE);
        
        -- Detect crossing
        IF is_inside AND NOT was_inside AND gf.entry_alert THEN
            INSERT INTO geofence_events (time, geofence_id, vehicle_id, event_type, location)
            VALUES (NEW.time, gf.id, NEW.vehicle_id, 'entry', ST_SetSRID(ST_MakePoint(NEW.longitude, NEW.latitude), 4326)::geography);
            
            INSERT INTO events (time, vehicle_id, event_type, severity, latitude, longitude, metadata)
            VALUES (NEW.time, NEW.vehicle_id, 'geofence_entry', 'info', NEW.latitude, NEW.longitude, 
                    jsonb_build_object('geofence_id', gf.id, 'geofence_name', gf.name));
                    
        ELSIF NOT is_inside AND was_inside AND gf.exit_alert THEN
            INSERT INTO geofence_events (time, geofence_id, vehicle_id, event_type, location)
            VALUES (NEW.time, gf.id, NEW.vehicle_id, 'exit', ST_SetSRID(ST_MakePoint(NEW.longitude, NEW.latitude), 4326)::geography);
            
            INSERT INTO events (time, vehicle_id, event_type, severity, latitude, longitude, metadata)
            VALUES (NEW.time, NEW.vehicle_id, 'geofence_exit', 'info', NEW.latitude, NEW.longitude,
                    jsonb_build_object('geofence_id', gf.id, 'geofence_name', gf.name));
        END IF;
    END LOOP;
    
    RETURN NEW;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;

CREATE TRIGGER trigger_check_geofence
    AFTER INSERT ON gps_readings
    FOR EACH ROW
    EXECUTE FUNCTION check_geofence_violation();
```

